    "reason": "[ev-27aaf3747c01] is a single changelog line saying repo URLs with `ssh`/`altssh` subdomains may now match the webhook payload. It doesn't say which resource field holds the matched repo URL, which URL forms or Git providers are affected, or how webhooks are set up. The proposed exposure treats the whole condition as runtime-only, but the repo URL is static configuration and should be checked by a predicate. Only whether webhooks actually arrive is runtime. The cited text doesn't give the field path or URL pattern needed to write that predicate, and the surrounding changelog items ([ev-d78886a20329] and others) add nothing on this subject. To settle the exposure we need the PR #21227 description or docs naming the repo URL field and the subdomain forms involved.",
